If extracted into a common function, it would look roughly like this:
```py
func mergeExtraBody(ctx context.Context, body []byte) ([]byte, *schemas.BifrostError) {
    if extraBody, ok := ctx.Value(schemas.BifrostContextKeyExtraBody).(map[string]any); ok && len(extraBody) > 0 {
        var err error
        body, err = MergeExtraParamsIntoJSON(body, extraBody)
        if err != nil {
            return nil, NewBifrostOperationError(schemas.ErrProviderRequestMarshal, err)
        }
    }
    return body, nil
}
```
This can eliminate the nearly identical 5 lines of code in two places, but the core logic is indeed two branches handling different input sources separately, not meaningless duplication.

